## Context
Parent: 1229. The mechanical half of the author's checklist, as a test in the
harness adherence gate, ratcheted against a baseline so existing debt warns
and new debt fails.

Checks over `skills/*/SKILL.md` and `skills/*/references/*.md`:
- body line count over 150: warning list (worklist for further splits), not a failure;
- fenced code blocks or heredocs over a small line threshold: the script
  belongs in `scripts/`;
- ticket numbers, merge-request numbers, dated filenames, project names;
- history phrasing (`phase N`, `since we`, `used to`, incident dates).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] One test module; `skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md` is the positive
      control and is flagged on line count, code-block length and history
- [ ] Baseline file records current debt; a new violation fails
- [ ] Project-name list is data, not hardcoded in the test
- [ ] Runs in the adherence command; no model call
